# Iron Linux - live medium + installer package list
#
# Packages that make the ISO behave as a live/bootable medium and let a
# user install Iron Linux to disk. live-boot/live-config/live-tools are
# effectively no-ops once installed to a real disk (they only activate
# with `boot=live` on the kernel command line), so it's safe to leave
# them in the installed system rather than special-case their removal.
#
# Calamares is the installer (see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md for why: mature,
# distribution-independent, Qt-based but not tied to KDE Plasma, and
# already has a Debian settings module we theme for Iron in a later task).

## --- Debian Live boot/session glue ---
live-boot
live-config
live-tools

## --- Installer ---
calamares
calamares-settings-debian
rsync
cryptsetup
keyutils
efibootmgr
os-prober
x11-xserver-utils
grub-pc-bin
grub-efi-amd64-bin
btrfs-progs
xfsprogs
